31
00:04:07.661 --> 00:04:17.926
soldiers&#8212;so many they resembled grasshoppers&#8212;fell upside down into the Sioux camp. The vision predicted victory, and it came true at the Battle of

32
00:04:17.927 --> 00:04:23.192
the Little Bighorn. On June 25, 1876, more than six hundred soldiers led by George Armstrong Custer attacked Sitting Bull’s village. Sioux

33
00:04:23.193 --> 00:04:32.132
warriors achieved a stunning victory, killing Custer and about two hundred of his men. Even though Custer had been the attacker, whites

34
00:04:32.133 --> 00:04:37.979
saw the battle as an atrocity and a massacre. Soldiers now harassed and attacked the Sioux at every opportunity, setting fire to

35
