up their freedom in exchange for peace, Sitting Bull still rejected life on a reservation. He took what was left of his

37
00:04:55.610 --> 00:05:02.981
followers to Canada, where the soldiers could not pursue them. They lived there until 1881, when, with the buffalo nearly extinct, Sitting

38
00:05:02.982 --> 00:05:08.113
Bull realized he must return to the United States to save his people from starvation. He was the last Native American chief to

39
00:05:08.114 --> 00:05:18.648
surrender to the U.S. government. Upon his return, Sitting Bull was treated as a prisoner of war for two years. Then, he

40
00:05:18.649 --> 00:05:28.143
was sent to Standing Rock Reservation, where he tried to adapt to white ways&#8212;farming the land and sending his children to school

41
00:05:28.144 --> 00:05:40.234
so they could learn to survive in the quickly changing world. He traveled throughout America, and for a few months, he even became

42
00:05:40.235 --> 00:05:51.295
